A||||2||Black88GT||Isolating culprit of squeeky suspension||||5||
Z||000000||Black88GT||05-12-2001||05:49 PM||||I thought for sure the reason why I was squeeking all the time was the rear sway bar bushings.  So I got them, installed them, still squeeking (poly - but I used a ton of that special grease).  OK, maybe its the front swaybar bushings.  Got them, installed them, still squeeking (again, used a lot of grease).  So is the only thing left the control arm bushings?  What else could it be?  I hope its not the control arm bushings.  It must be related to the weather because once the weather warmed up it squeeked like crazy.  Do the poly bushings need some "breaking in"?  I only took a ride around the block each time after I installed the bushings.<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||05-12-2001||06:13 PM||||Poly squeeks. There's no way around that. <P>You need to find someone to bounce the car while you look and listen.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||05-12-2001||07:57 PM||||On the 88's, if the nuts on the top of the front shock shafts are not tight enough, it will squeak all friggin day long. Took me a month to figure out where it was coming from. Tightened em down till the bushing was nice and squished, haven't heard a peep since.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
